.TITLE "type"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays the contents of one or more text files. It outputs the raw text to the command prompt window without modification.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**type file.txt**
Displays the content of the specified text file.
> __file.txt__ the target file name

**type file1.txt file2.txt**
Displays the contents of multiple files sequentially.
> 

**type file.txt | more**
Displays the content of a large file one screen at a time.
> __| more__ pagination pipe

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __type__ is a quick way to inspect log files or configuration data without opening a full text editor. For very large files, always pipe the output to **windows:more** to avoid being overwhelmed by text.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:echo** **windows:dir**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/type__
